{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.TauNormalizationChoice","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.TauNormalizationChoice","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.QBeta.ObservableComplexVolumeVsFullPotential"],"declarations":5,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.TauNormalizationChoice.full_potential_and_Aomega_three_incompatible","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.TauNormalizationChoice.full_potential_and_Aomega_three_incompatible","kind":"theorem","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/TauNormalizationChoice.lean#L75-L85","doc":"Application: the two live corpus conventions (`Φ`, i.e. `A = 2`, and the\n`A_ω = 3` target) are incompatible on any channel with a nonvanishing point —\nthe reconciliation (`qou-pzzl`) must retire one, and which one is exactly the\nopen `qou-yh67` binary. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.TauNormalizationChoice.dressing_factor_unique","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.TauNormalizationChoice.dressing_factor_unique","kind":"theorem","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/TauNormalizationChoice.lean#L64-L73","doc":"**Exclusivity.** Two dressings of the same channel with the same\ndeformation agree everywhere, so at any point where the channel's geometric\npart does not vanish the dressing factors are equal. This is the precise\nform of \"one of the two conventions is wrong\": `A = 2` (full potential) and\n`A = 3` (the `A_ω` target) cannot both hold at a nonvanishing point. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.TauNormalizationChoice.usesFullPotential_iff_A_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.TauNormalizationChoice.usesFullPotential_iff_A_two","kind":"theorem","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/TauNormalizationChoice.lean#L55-L62","doc":"The full-potential convention IS the complex-volume convention with the\ninteger forced to `2` — the `qou-pzzl` \"two conventions\" are one integer\nvariable. Direct from `Φ = 2𝔙`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.TauNormalizationChoice.UsesFullPotentialNorm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.TauNormalizationChoice.UsesFullPotentialNorm","kind":"def","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/TauNormalizationChoice.lean#L50-L53","doc":"The channel `S` carries the full-potential normalization\n`S q = Im Φ(u q)` (no dressing factor). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.TauNormalizationChoice.UsesComplexVolumeNorm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.TauNormalizationChoice.UsesComplexVolumeNorm","kind":"def","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/TauNormalizationChoice.lean#L44-L48","doc":"The channel `S` carries the complex-volume normalization dressed by the\nreal factor `A`: `S q = A · Im 𝔙(u q)` at every substrate value. The open\nquestion (qou-yh67) is WHICH `A` the τ-functor applies. ","signatureChunk":0}]}